# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors / IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Node (the plugin has zero dependencies today; this is for if that changes —
# note package-lock.json should be committed, not ignored)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Logs
*.log

# Local runtime state.
#
# The plugin never writes into its own directory at runtime — all state lives in
# ~/.claude/smart-thinking/, because ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} is version-stamped and
# reaped a couple of weeks after an update. These patterns exist only to catch
# stray output from testing with CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR pointed at the repo.
#
# Leading slash anchors each to the repo root. Unanchored, "config.json" would
# also swallow data/config.json or lib/config.json in future.
/cache.json
/config.json
/deck.json
/learn-state.json
/settings.backup.json
/refresh.log

# NOTE: do not add a blanket dot-file rule such as ".*" — it would exclude
# .claude-plugin/, which holds plugin.json and marketplace.json. Without those
# the repo is not a plugin and not a marketplace.
#
# NOTE: never ignore bin/. Here it is hand-written source, not build output.
# Most language templates (Go, Java, .NET) ignore bin/ by default, so pasting
# one in would silently gut the plugin: the SessionStart hook, the status line,
# and all five slash commands invoke bin/*.js by path. Same goes for lib/ and
# providers/ — nothing in this repo is generated, so nothing is safe to drop.
